// Chapter 4 — the endings. Shows faction gates, triggers (guild-wary in story.talewright.yaml),
// conditional diverts and several endings.

=== ending.return
@title The Return

The walk back to camp is quiet. {guide:first-name} keeps glancing at your pack.

{if player has relic}
* [Hand the relic to the guild] (requires: faction:explorers-guild >= neutral) { take player relic; faction:explorers-guild += 20 } -> ending.guild
* [Keep it for yourself] { faction:explorers-guild -= 30 } -> ending.keep
{/if}

-> ending.empty-handed

=== ending.guild
@title Honoured

The {faction:explorers-guild:name} hangs {player:last-name#possessive} portrait in the great hall, a little
crooked. Your standing with them is now *{faction:explorers-guild:tier#lower}*.
{if player has idol}
Nobody asks about the {item:idol} on your desk.
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.keep
@title The Keeper

You keep the {item:relic}. It keeps you, too: you sleep less, and dream of a door with a closed eye.
{if flag:guild-wary}
The guild's letters stop coming. Then the guild's people start coming instead.
// Nested conditionals and a compound and/or test. Blocks nest to any depth; `and` binds tighter than `or`,
// and parentheses group as usual.
{if player:level >= 2 and (player has idol or visited(temple.side))}
You meet them at the door, rested and unhurried{if player has idol}, the {item:idol} watching from the
mantel behind you{/if}. They leave without the relic, and never quite work out why.
{else}
You start sleeping with the relic under your pillow.
{/if}
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.empty-handed
@title Empty-Handed

You return with nothing but {player:pronoun#possessive} notes and a story nobody at the guild quite
believes. {guide:first-name}, at least, buys you a drink.
-> END
